---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Upstream dashboard issue and actionable PRs (nightly CI)

Usage: odx bot [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  run        The nightly cycle: act on the ticked boxes, then update the dashboard issue
  dashboard  Only update the dashboard issue; ticked boxes stay ticked
  act        Only act on the boxes ticked in the dashboard issue (for `issues` events)
  plan       What `odx bot run` would do, as JSON; writes nothing
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml to use (a repos.yaml for the commands that read one)

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve forge and index data from the cache only; a repository not in the cache yet is still fetched. Local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only
